<td id="S2.T2.1.20.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">
<span id="S2.T2.1.20.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="S2.T2.1.20.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">Index of a transition sample in the buffer; the batch size</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S2.T2.1.21" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S2.T2.1.21.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row"><math id="S2.T2.m33" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E},L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E},L</annotation></semantics></math></th>
<td id="S2.T2.1.21.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">
<span id="S2.T2.1.21.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="S2.T2.1.21.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">Number of episodes; number of iterations in <em id="S2.T2.1.21.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">EPOS</em></span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S2.T2.1.22" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S2.T2.1.22.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row"><math id="S2.T2.m34" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{\text{dnn}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mtext>dnn</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\text{dnn}}</annotation></semantics></math></th>
<td id="S2.T2.1.22.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">
<span id="S2.T2.1.22.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="S2.T2.1.22.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">Computational complexity of deep neutral networks</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S2.T2.1.23" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S2.T2.1.23.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row"><math id="S2.T2.m35" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W</annotation></semantics></math></th>
<td id="S2.T2.1.23.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">
<span id="S2.T2.1.23.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="S2.T2.1.23.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">Number of nodes per layer in deep neutral networks</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S2.T2.1.24" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S2.T2.1.24.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_b"><math id="S2.T2.m36" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma,\hat{A},\hat{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma,\hat{A},\hat{C}</annotation></semantics></math></th>
<td id="S2.T2.1.24.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_b">
<span id="S2.T2.1.24.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="S2.T2.1.24.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">Discount factor; advantage function; surrogate loss function</span>
</span></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S3" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">III </span><span id="S3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">System Model</span></h2>

<div id="S3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, the decentralized combinatorial optimization problem in evolving multi-agent systems is modeled as a sequential decision-making. It involves the definition of plans, as well as modeling of individual and system-wide costs.</p>
</div>
<section id="S3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S3.SS1.4" class="ltx_text">III-A</span> </span><span id="S3.SS1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Problem Statement</span></h3>

<div id="S3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The core problem is how to coordinate multiple agents to select their operations (i.e., decision-making) among alternatives (i.e., <span id="S3.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">possible operational plans</span>) such that they complete system-wide tasks efficiently over a long time span (e.g., an full-day mission).</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Each option, referred to as a possible operational <em id="S3.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">plan</em>, represents a sequence of tasks scheduled over a specific time period for execution. This planning-based model is particularly powerful because each plan encapsulates a full operation cycle, allowing agents/drones to reason at a higher level of abstraction. First, by having a complete overview of a potential trip, each drone can accurately estimate its energy consumption in advance, enabling more reliable and energy-aware decision-making. Second, since each discrete plan represents an extended operation, often lasting over 30 minutes, drones avoid making decisions at every minute or second. This significantly reduces the complexity of the decision space and allows the system to scale efficiently, even in large and dynamic environments.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">In this problem, a plan of agent <math id="S3.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> at a time period <math id="S3.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> is defined as <math id="S3.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{u}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>u</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{u}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\forall u\in\mathcal{U}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\forall u\in\mathcal{U}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.SS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\forall t\in\mathcal{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\forall t\in\mathcal{T}</annotation></semantics></math>. It is a sequence of real values (i.e., a vector) and generated based on the current environment observed by <math id="S3.SS1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math>, formulated as follows:</p>
<table id="S3.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{u}_{kt}=(p^{u}_{ktd})_{d=1}^{D}=f_{p}(\tau_{t},c^{u}_{t})\in\mathcal{P}^{u}_{t}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>D</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>u</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{u}_{kt}=(p^{u}_{ktd})_{d=1}^{D}=f_{p}(\tau_{t},c^{u}_{t})\in\mathcal{P}^{u}_{t},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the position index of a value inside a plan with the size of <math id="S3.SS1.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math>; <math id="S3.SS1.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}^{u}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>u</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}^{u}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the set of plans generated by <math id="S3.SS1.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> at <math id="S3.SS1.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>; <math id="S3.SS1.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> is the index of plan in <math id="S3.SS1.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}^{u}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>u</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}^{u}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.SS1.p3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\leq K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\leq K</annotation></semantics></math>; <math id="S3.SS1.p3.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{p}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{p}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> represents the plan generation function that produces plans of an agent; <math id="S3.SS1.p3.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> indicates the <span id="S3.SS1.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">target tasks</span> required for agents to complete at <math id="S3.SS1.p3.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, such as the required amount of data collected by drones; <math id="S3.SS1.p3.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c^{u}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>u</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c^{u}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the environmental constraints on agent <math id="S3.SS1.p3.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math>, e.g., the flight range of drones. At each time period, the systems evolve such that the target and constraints require adaptation.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Each agent selects one and only one plan <math id="S3.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{u}_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>u</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{u}_{s}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\leq K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\leq K</annotation></semantics></math>, which is referred to as the <span id="S3.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">selected plan</span> (i.e. the agent’s choice). All agents’ choices aggregate element-wise to the collective choice, i.e., the <em id="S3.SS1.p4.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">global plan</em> <math id="S3.SS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> of the multi-agent system, formulated as follows:</p>
<table id="S3.E2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{t}=(g_{td})_{d=1}^{D}=\sum_{u\in\mathcal{U}}p^{u}_{st}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>D</mi></msubsup><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi></mrow></munder><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>u</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{t}=(g_{td})_{d=1}^{D}=\sum_{u\in\mathcal{U}}p^{u}_{st}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S3.SS2.4" class="ltx_text">III-B</span> </span><span id="S3.SS2.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Problem Formulation</span></h3>

<div id="S3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Based on the design of plans, the problem is defined by two objectives:</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">One is to minimize the individual cost of agents, which is formulated by the <span id="S3.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">discomfort cost function</span> <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{d}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{d}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math>: It indicates the discomfort cost <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D^{u}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>u</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D^{u}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> incurred by an agent executing a specific plan, e.g., the energy consumption of a drone flight path. The objective function for the <span id="S3.SS2.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">mean discomfort cost</span> denotes the time-accumulated average discomfort cost of selected plans per agent over all time periods. It is formulated as follows:</p>
<table id="S3.E3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathop{\min}\limits_{p^{u}_{st}}\;\sum_{t\in\mathcal{T}}\frac{\sum_{u\in\mathcal{U}}D^{u}_{t}}{U}=\sum_{t\in\mathcal{T}}\frac{\sum_{u\in\mathcal{U}}f_{d}(p^{u}_{st})}{U}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">min</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>u</mi></msubsup></munder><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></mrow></munder><mfrac><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi></mrow></msub><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>u</mi></msubsup></mrow><mi>U</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></mrow></munder><mfrac><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mi>U</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathop{\min}\limits_{p^{u}_{st}}\;\sum_{t\in\mathcal{T}}\frac{\sum_{u\in\mathcal{U}}D^{u}_{t}}{U}=\sum_{t\in\mathcal{T}}\frac{\sum_{u\in\mathcal{U}}f_{d}(p^{u}_{st})}{U}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The other objective is to minimize the system-wide cost, which is formulated by the <span id="S3.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">inefficiency cost function</span> <math id="S3.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{i}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{i}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math>: It aims to match the global plan of agents to the target of system, e.g., reducing the root mean square error. Since this cost function is non-linear, meaning the choices of the agents depend on each other, minimizing the inefficiency cost is a combinatorial NP-hard optimization problem <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">2</a>]</cite>. Therefore, the objective function of inefficiency cost <math id="S3.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is expressed as:</p>
<table id="S3.E4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathop{\min}\limits_{p^{u}_{st}}\;\sum_{t\in\mathcal{T}}I_{t}=\sum_{t\in\mathcal{T}}f_{i}(\tau_{t},g_{t})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">min</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>u</mi></msubsup></munder><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathop{\min}\limits_{p^{u}_{st}}\;\sum_{t\in\mathcal{T}}I_{t}=\sum_{t\in\mathcal{T}}f_{i}(\tau_{t},g_{t}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Satisfying all of these (opposing) objectives depends on the selfish vs. altruistic behavior of the agents, e.g. whether they accept a plan with a bit higher discomfort cost to decrease inefficiency cost. Such multi-objective trade-offs are modeled as follows:</p>
<table id="S3.E5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathop{\min}\limits_{p^{u}_{st}}\;\beta^{u}_{t}\cdot D^{u}_{t}+(1-\beta^{u}_{t})\cdot I_{t}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">min</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>u</mi></msubsup></munder><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>u</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>u</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>u</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathop{\min}\limits_{p^{u}_{st}}\;\beta^{u}_{t}\cdot D^{u}_{t}+(1-\beta^{u}_{t})\cdot I_{t},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p4.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta^{u}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>u</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta^{u}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> represents the behavior of the agent <math id="S3.SS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> to balance both discomfort and inefficiency cost, <math id="S3.SS2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq\beta^{u}_{t}\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq\beta^{u}_{t}\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math>. As the value of <math id="S3.SS2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta^{u}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>u</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta^{u}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> increases, the agent becomes more selfish, prioritizing plans with low discomfort cost at the expense of higher inefficiency cost.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S3.F1" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2509.18088v1/HierarchicalFramework.png" id="S3.F1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:476/483;" width="476" height="483" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Fig. 1: </span>The system framework of <em id="S3.F1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">HRCL</em>.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S4" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">IV </span><span id="S4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Proposed Method</span></h2>

<div id="S4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The proposed method of <span id="S4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">HRCL</span> is presented in this section. According to Eq.(<a href="#S3.E5" title="In III-B Problem Formulation ‣ III System Model ‣ Strategic Coordination for Evolving Multi-agent Systems:A Hierarchical Reinforcement and Collective Learning Approach" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>), agents’ plan selection is determined by two factors: their local plans and behavior. Generating plans with low cost or choosing a selfish behavior can lead to lower mean discomfort cost but higher inefficiency cost and vice versa. Therefore, <em id="S4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">HRCL</em> determines high-level action choices of the agents among (1) what alternatives they decide and (2) what behavior/preference they use to decide. Two types of strategies are employed respectively: <span id="S4.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">grouping plan constraints</span> and <span id="S4.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">grouping behavior ranges</span>. The former strategy divides the constraints of plans into different groups based on a criterion, e.g., the range of discomfort cost or the flight range of drones, and then chooses one of them. The latter strategy divides behavior <math id="S4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta^{u}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>u</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta^{u}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> into ranges and chooses one to balance discomfort and inefficiency costs.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Fig.<a href="#S3.F1" title="Fig. 1 ‣ III-B Problem Formulation ‣ III System Model ‣ Strategic Coordination for Evolving Multi-agent Systems:A Hierarchical Reinforcement and Collective Learning Approach" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> illustrates the overall framework of <em id="S4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">HRCL</em>. First, at a time period <math id="S4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, all agents construct into a tree topology where the root agent receives the initial target task <math id="S4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> from the server and then sends it to other agents via top-down phase, which will be illustrated in Section <a href="#S4.SS3" title="IV-C Low-level Plan Selection ‣ IV Proposed Method ‣ Strategic Coordination for Evolving Multi-agent Systems:A Hierarchical Reinforcement and Collective Learning Approach" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">IV-C</span></a>. Next, each agent takes a high-level action, the results of choosing a plan constraint (grouping plan constraints) and a behavior range (grouping behavior ranges). Then, in the low-level layer, each agent generates plans via Eq.(<a href="#S3.E1" title="In III-A Problem Statement ‣ III System Model ‣ Strategic Coordination for Evolving Multi-agent Systems:A Hierarchical Reinforcement and Collective Learning Approach" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>) based on the chosen constraint. Next, each agent coordinates to select its optimal plan based on the chosen behavior and obtains the global plan via collective learning or exact algorithms. Agents will execute their selected plans, which changes the environmental state and updates the target tasks in the next time period <math id="S4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{t+1}\leftarrow\tau_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{t+1}\leftarrow\tau_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>. Furthermore, the global plan is used for reward calculation calculation and state transition defined in Section <a href="#S4.SS1" title="IV-A MARL modeling ‣ IV Proposed Method ‣ Strategic Coordination for Evolving Multi-agent Systems:A Hierarchical Reinforcement and Collective Learning Approach" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">IV-A</span></a>. The state, action and reward of each agent are stored into a replay buffer in order to train the parameters of deep neutral networks in agents’ policy, assisting them to explore optimized actions.</p>
</div>
<section id="S4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S4.SS1.4" class="ltx_text">IV-A</span> </span><span id="S4.SS1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">MARL modeling</span></h3>

<div id="S4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">At each time period, each agent observes the global plan, makes a decision on its new plan and updates the global plan, which serves as its observation in the next time period. Besides, the target tasks updates as the systems evolve. Thus, the problem can be modeled as a Markov decision process <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib30" title="" class="ltx_ref">30</a>]</cite>. We model the problem using the concepts of state, action and reward:</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">State.</span>
The state <math id="S4.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S^{u}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>u</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S^{u}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> includes the information observed by an agent <math id="S4.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math>, such as the target <math id="S4.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, the selected plan <math id="S4.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{u}_{st}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>u</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{u}_{st}</annotation></semantics></math>, the global plan <math id="S4.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, and the discomfort costs of all selected plans <math id="S4.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D^{u}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>u</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D^{u}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Action.</span>
The action <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{u}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>u</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{u}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> of agent <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> at <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> is denoted as <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{u}_{t}=(a^{u}_{imt})_{i\leq I,m\leq M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{u}_{t}=(a^{u}_{imt})_{i\leq I,m\leq M}</annotation></semantics></math>, where the agent <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> chooses a constraint index <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>I</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I</annotation></semantics></math> constraints of plans, and a behavior range index <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> ranges (see Section <a href="#S4.SS2" title="IV-B High-level Strategies ‣ IV Proposed Method ‣ Strategic Coordination for Evolving Multi-agent Systems:A Hierarchical Reinforcement and Collective Learning Approach" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">IV-B</span></a>). In addition, the state of agent <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> transitions from <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S^{u}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>u</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S^{u}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S^{u}_{t+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>u</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S^{u}_{t+1}</annotation></semantics></math> after executing the action <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{u}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>u</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{u}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> and selecting a new plan <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{u}_{st}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>u</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{u}_{st}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Reward.</span>
The expected immediate reward of an agent is calculated based on the combined cost, indicating the sum of the normalized mean discomfort cost and inefficiency cost. According to the objective functions in Eq.(<a href="#S3.E3" title="In III-B Problem Formulation ‣ III System Model ‣ Strategic Coordination for Evolving Multi-agent Systems:A Hierarchical Reinforcement and Collective Learning Approach" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>) and Eq.(<a href="#S3.E4" title="In III-B Problem Formulation ‣ III System Model ‣ Strategic Coordination for Evolving Multi-agent Systems:A Hierarchical Reinforcement and Collective Learning Approach" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>), the reward function at each time period <math id="S4.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> is expressed as:</p>
<table id="S4.E6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E6.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="R^{u}_{t}=-\sigma_{1}\cdot\frac{1}{U}\cdot\sum_{u\in\mathcal{U}}D^{u}_{t}-\sigma_{2}\cdot I_{t}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>u</mi></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>σ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>U</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.055em">⋅</mo><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi></mrow></msub><mi>D</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>u</mi></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>σ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>I</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R^{u}_{t}=-\sigma_{1}\cdot\frac{1}{U}\cdot\sum_{u\in\mathcal{U}}D^{u}_{t}-\sigma_{2}\cdot I_{t}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS1.p4.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S4.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> are the parameters set by the system to normalize the discomfort and inefficiency cost respectively, <math id="S4.SS1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{1},\sigma_{2}\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{1},\sigma_{2}\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S4.SS2.4" class="ltx_text">IV-B</span> </span><span id="S4.SS2.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">High-level Strategies</span></h3>

<div id="S4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The high-level actions provide strategic guidance and constraints, shaping the discomfort cost of low-level actions to ensure that they align with overall objectives and efficiently achieve the optimization goals. The action consists of two strategies for group choices: the <em id="S4.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">grouping plan constraints</em> and the <em id="S4.SS2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">grouping behavior ranges</em>.</p>
</div>
<section id="S4.SS2.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection"><span id="S4.SS2.SSS1.4" class="ltx_text">IV-B</span>1 </span>Strategy for grouping plan constraints</h4>

<div id="S4.SS2.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The key idea of this strategy is to divide the constraints of all possible plans into multiple groups based on a criterion, which could be the discomfort cost of plans, or the flight range of drones that perform tasking. By choosing one constraint, each agent generates the plans under the constraint and selects a plan from them. Since agents only takes action to choose a group, i.e., a constraint of plans, instead of selecting a plan from the entire set <math id="S4.SS2.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}^{u}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>u</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}^{u}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, each agent significantly reduces the number of available action choices, thereby reducing the action space. The selection of plan constraints can be defined as:</p>
<table id="S4.E7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E7.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\{p^{u}_{ijt},\;\forall j\leq G_{i}\}\leftarrow A^{u}_{t}\;|\;A^{u}_{t}=a^{u}_{imt}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.447em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{p^{u}_{ijt},\;\forall j\leq G_{i}\}\leftarrow A^{u}_{t}\;|\;A^{u}_{t}=a^{u}_{imt},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.SSS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S4.SS2.SSS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the index of a constraint within a total of <math id="S4.SS2.SSS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>I</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I</annotation></semantics></math> constraints, <math id="S4.SS2.SSS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math> implies the index of a plan under the constraint <math id="S4.SS2.SSS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S4.SS2.SSS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is the total number of plans under constraint <math id="S4.SS2.SSS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.SS2.SSS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{i}\leq K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{i}\leq K</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS2.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection"><span id="S4.SS2.SSS2.4" class="ltx_text">IV-B</span>2 </span>Strategy for grouping behavior ranges</h4>

<div id="S4.SS2.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This strategy is designed to select from a group of behavior range rather than choosing among all possible values. The entire range <math id="S4.SS2.SSS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> splits into <math id="S4.SS2.SSS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> non-overlapping ranges of equal length, each range with an index of <math id="S4.SS2.SSS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, each agent takes an action <math id="S4.SS2.SSS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{u}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>u</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{u}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> to choose a range, and sets the mean value of the range as the agent’s behavior <math id="S4.SS2.SSS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta^{u}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>u</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta^{u}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>. The strategy can be formulated as:</p>
<table id="S4.E8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta^{u}_{t}=\frac{m}{M}-\frac{1}{2M}\;|\;A^{u}_{t}=a^{u}_{imt}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>m</mi><mi>M</mi></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false" lspace="0.558em">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>u</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta^{u}_{t}=\frac{m}{M}-\frac{1}{2M}\;|\;A^{u}_{t}=a^{u}_{imt}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<figure id="S4.F2" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2509.18088v1/PlanSelection.png" id="S4.F2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/270;" width="476" height="270" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Fig. 2: </span>The learning iteration in the low-level plan selection. During the bottom-up phase, Agent 3 aggregates the plans of its children, i.e., Agent 1 and Agent 2, and sends them to its parent agent with its own plan. During the top-down phase, each parent agent sends the global plan and a decision to approve/reject the plan selection to its children.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S4.SS3.4" class="ltx_text">IV-C</span> </span><span id="S4.SS3.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Low-level Plan Selection</span></h3>

<div id="S4.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Following the high-level strategies, each agent selects an optimal plan from the ones it generates using decentralized collective learning <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">2</a>, <a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">3</a>, <a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">13</a>]</cite>. This method uses a tree communication topology to structure the agents’ interactions. Agents connect into the tree structure within which they iteratively interact with their children and parent, i.e, the neighboring agents, in order to observe and aggregate the plans efficiently to perform decisions.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">In this settings, the system can dynamically reconfigure, repositioning agents within the tree in response to communication failures, ensuring that a single agent failure has minimal impact on information flow. The resilience has been previously demonstrated with large-scale real-world datasets <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib31" title="" class="ltx_ref">31</a>]</cite>. Additional privacy protection mechanisms, such as differential privacy and homomorphic encryption, also apply <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib32" title="" class="ltx_ref">32</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">As shown in Fig. <a href="#S4.F2" title="Fig. 2 ‣ IV-B2 Strategy for grouping behavior ranges ‣ IV-B High-level Strategies ‣ IV Proposed Method ‣ Strategic Coordination for Evolving Multi-agent Systems:A Hierarchical Reinforcement and Collective Learning Approach" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, the communication process at each iteration contains two phases: bottom-up and top-down. During the bottom-up phase, each agent (except for leaf nodes) aggregates the plans of its children and selects its own plan via Eq.(<a href="#S3.E5" title="In III-B Problem Formulation ‣ III System Model ‣ Strategic Coordination for Evolving Multi-agent Systems:A Hierarchical Reinforcement and Collective Learning Approach" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>). Then, the agent combines the selected plan with the aggregated plans from its children and shares this aggregated information to its parent node (if it is not the root). As a result, the root node aggregates the plans of all agents and obtains the global plan. During the top-down process, however, each agent (except for leaf nodes) sends feedback to its children, including the global plan <math id="S4.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> and a decision <math id="S4.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta^{u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>δ</mi><mi>u</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta^{u}</annotation></semantics></math> regarding whether to approve the plan selection of its children in the current iteration. The decision is calculated by comparing the inefficiency cost based on the selected plan of child agent in the current iteration with the outcome in the previous iteration <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">2</a>]</cite>. An agent node will adopt the new selected plan if approved by its parent (<math id="S4.SS3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta^{u}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>δ</mi><mi>u</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta^{u}=1</annotation></semantics></math>), i.e., the current inefficiency cost is lower than previous one. Otherwise, it keeps the plan selected in the previous iteration. Finally, all agents store the global plan for the next iteration.</p>
</div>
<figure id="alg1" class="ltx_float ltx_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span><em id="alg1.4" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">HRCL</em> Training.</figcaption>
<div id="alg1.5" class="ltx_listing ltx_lst_numbers_left ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg1.5.1" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="alg1.5.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">
Randomly initialize critic network <math id="alg1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math>, actor network <math id="alg1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> with weights <math id="alg1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta^{Q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>θ</mi><mi>Q</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta^{Q}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta^{\pi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>θ</mi><mi>π</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta^{\pi}</annotation></semantics></math>;</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.5.2" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.5.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">1</span></span>
            <span id="alg1.5.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">for</span><span id="alg1.5.2.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;"> </span><em id="alg1.5.2.4" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:80%;">episode <math id="alg1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext=":=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">:=1</annotation></semantics></math> to max-episode-number</em><span id="alg1.5.2.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;"> </span><span id="alg1.5.2.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">do</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.5.3" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="alg1.5.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">  </span><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span><span id="alg1.5.3.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">  </span>
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.5.3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">2</span></span>
            <span id="alg1.5.3.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">Reset the target </span><math id="alg1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathsize="0.800em">τ</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{t}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.5.3.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;"> and the state of agents;</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.5.4" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="alg1.5.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">  </span><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span><span id="alg1.5.4.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">  </span>
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.5.4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">3</span></span>
            <span id="alg1.5.4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">for</span><span id="alg1.5.4.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;"> </span><em id="alg1.5.4.6" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:80%;">period <math id="alg1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t:=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>:=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t:=1</annotation></semantics></math> to max-episode-length</em><span id="alg1.5.4.7" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;"> </span><span id="alg1.5.4.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">do</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.5.5" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="alg1.5.5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">  </span><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span><span id="alg1.5.5.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">    </span><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span><span id="alg1.5.5.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">  </span>
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.5.5.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">4</span></span>
            <span id="alg1.5.5.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">for</span><span id="alg1.5.5.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;"> </span><em id="alg1.5.5.7" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:80%;"><math id="alg1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\forall u\in\mathcal{U}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\forall u\in\mathcal{U}</annotation></semantics></math></em><span id="alg1.5.5.8" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;"> </span><span id="alg1.5.5.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">do</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.5.6" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="alg1.5.6.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">  </span><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span><span id="alg1.5.6.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">    </span><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span><span id="alg1.5.6.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">    </span><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span><span id="alg1.5.6.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">  </span>
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.5.6.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">5</span></span>
            <span id="alg1.5.6.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">Take action: </span><math id="alg1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{u}_{t}=\pi(S^{u}_{t}|\theta^{\pi})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.800em">A</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">t</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">u</mi></msubsup><mo mathsize="0.800em">=</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">(</mo><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.800em">S</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">t</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">u</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.800em">θ</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">π</mi></msup><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{u}_{t}=\pi(S^{u}_{t}|\theta^{\pi})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.5.6.7" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">;</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.5.7" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="alg1.5.7.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">  </span><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span><span id="alg1.5.7.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">    </span><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span><span id="alg1.5.7.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">    </span><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span><span id="alg1.5.7.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">  </span>
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.5.7.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">6</span></span>
            <span id="alg1.5.7.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">Grouping plan constraints and choose </span><math id="alg1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c^{u}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.800em">c</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">t</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">u</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c^{u}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.5.7.7" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;"> via Eq.(</span><a href="#S4.E7" title="In IV-B1 Strategy for grouping plan constraints ‣ IV-B High-level Strategies ‣ IV Proposed Method ‣ Strategic Coordination for Evolving Multi-agent Systems:A Hierarchical Reinforcement and Collective Learning Approach" class="ltx_ref" style="font-size:80%;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a><span id="alg1.5.7.8" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">);</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.5.8" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="alg1.5.8.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">  </span><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span><span id="alg1.5.8.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">    </span><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span><span id="alg1.5.8.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">    </span><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span><span id="alg1.5.8.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">  </span>
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.5.8.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">7</span></span>
