<div id="alg2.5.3" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.5.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">2</span></span>
            <span id="alg2.5.3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">for</span><span id="alg2.5.3.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;"> </span><em id="alg2.5.3.4" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:80%;">period <math id="alg2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t:=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>:=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t:=1</annotation></semantics></math> to max-episode-length</em><span id="alg2.5.3.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;"> </span><span id="alg2.5.3.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">do</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.5.4" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="alg2.5.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">  </span><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span><span id="alg2.5.4.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">  </span>
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.5.4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">3</span></span>
            <span id="alg2.5.4.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">Update the target </span><math id="alg2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathsize="0.800em">τ</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{t}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg2.5.4.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;"> and the state;</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.5.5" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="alg2.5.5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">  </span><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span><span id="alg2.5.5.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">  </span>
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.5.5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">4</span></span>
            <span id="alg2.5.5.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">Generate plans based on the environment via Eq.(</span><a href="#S3.E1" title="In III-A Problem Statement ‣ III System Model ‣ Strategic Coordination for Evolving Multi-agent Systems:A Hierarchical Reinforcement and Collective Learning Approach" class="ltx_ref" style="font-size:80%;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a><span id="alg2.5.5.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">);</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.5.6" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="alg2.5.6.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">  </span><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span><span id="alg2.5.6.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">  </span>
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.5.6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">5</span></span>
            <span id="alg2.5.6.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">Take action: </span><math id="alg2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{u}_{t}=\pi(S^{u}_{t}|\theta^{\pi})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.800em">A</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">t</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">u</mi></msubsup><mo mathsize="0.800em">=</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">(</mo><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.800em">S</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">t</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">u</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.800em">θ</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">π</mi></msup><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{u}_{t}=\pi(S^{u}_{t}|\theta^{\pi})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg2.5.6.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">;</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.5.7" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="alg2.5.7.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">  </span><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span><span id="alg2.5.7.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">  </span>
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.5.7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">6</span></span>
            <span id="alg2.5.7.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">Grouping plans and choose a group via Eq.(</span><a href="#S4.E7" title="In IV-B1 Strategy for grouping plan constraints ‣ IV-B High-level Strategies ‣ IV Proposed Method ‣ Strategic Coordination for Evolving Multi-agent Systems:A Hierarchical Reinforcement and Collective Learning Approach" class="ltx_ref" style="font-size:80%;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a><span id="alg2.5.7.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">);</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.5.8" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="alg2.5.8.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">  </span><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span><span id="alg2.5.8.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">  </span>
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.5.8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">7</span></span>
            <span id="alg2.5.8.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">Grouping behavior ranges and choose a sub-range via Eq.(</span><a href="#S4.E8" title="In IV-B2 Strategy for grouping behavior ranges ‣ IV-B High-level Strategies ‣ IV Proposed Method ‣ Strategic Coordination for Evolving Multi-agent Systems:A Hierarchical Reinforcement and Collective Learning Approach" class="ltx_ref" style="font-size:80%;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a><span id="alg2.5.8.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">);</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.5.9" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="alg2.5.9.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">  </span><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span><span id="alg2.5.9.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">  </span>
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.5.9.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">8</span></span>
            <span id="alg2.5.9.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">for</span><span id="alg2.5.9.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;"> </span><em id="alg2.5.9.6" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:80%;">iteration <math id="alg2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext=":=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">:=1</annotation></semantics></math> to max-iteration-number</em><span id="alg2.5.9.7" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;"> </span><span id="alg2.5.9.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">do</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.5.10" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="alg2.5.10.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">  </span><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span><span id="alg2.5.10.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">    </span><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span><span id="alg2.5.10.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">  </span>
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.5.10.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">9</span></span>
            <span id="alg2.5.10.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">Aggregate the plans of children and determine decision </span><math id="alg2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta^{u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi mathsize="0.800em">δ</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">u</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta^{u}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg2.5.10.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">;</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.5.11" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="alg2.5.11.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">  </span><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span><span id="alg2.5.11.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">    </span><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span><span id="alg2.5.11.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">  </span>
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.5.11.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">10</span></span>
            <span id="alg2.5.11.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">Select a plan </span><math id="alg2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{u}_{st}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.800em">p</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">t</mi></mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">u</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{u}_{st}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg2.5.11.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;"> via Eq.(</span><a href="#S3.E5" title="In III-B Problem Formulation ‣ III System Model ‣ Strategic Coordination for Evolving Multi-agent Systems:A Hierarchical Reinforcement and Collective Learning Approach" class="ltx_ref" style="font-size:80%;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a><span id="alg2.5.11.7" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">);</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.5.12" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="alg2.5.12.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">  </span><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span><span id="alg2.5.12.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">    </span><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span><span id="alg2.5.12.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">  </span>
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.5.12.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">11</span></span>
            <span id="alg2.5.12.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">Share the aggregated plans and selected plan to parent;</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.5.13" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="alg2.5.13.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">  </span><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span><span id="alg2.5.13.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">    </span><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span><span id="alg2.5.13.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">  </span>
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.5.13.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">12</span></span>
            <span id="alg2.5.13.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">Wait for the decision and the global plan </span><math id="alg2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathsize="0.800em">g</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{t}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg2.5.13.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;"> from parent;</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.5.14" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="alg2.5.14.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">  </span><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span><span id="alg2.5.14.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">    </span><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span><span id="alg2.5.14.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">  </span>
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.5.14.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">13</span></span>
            <span id="alg2.5.14.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">Send </span><math id="alg2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta^{u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi mathsize="0.800em">δ</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">u</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta^{u}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg2.5.14.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;"> and </span><math id="alg2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathsize="0.800em">g</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{t}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg2.5.14.7" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;"> to children;</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.5.15" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="alg2.5.15.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">  </span><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span><span id="alg2.5.15.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">  </span>
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.5.15.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">14</span></span>
            <span id="alg2.5.15.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">end for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.5.16" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.5.16.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">15</span></span>
            <span id="alg2.5.16.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">end for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.5.17" class="ltx_listingline">
</div>
</div>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S4.SS4.4" class="ltx_text">IV-D</span> </span><span id="S4.SS4.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">MARL Training and Execution</span></h3>

<div id="S4.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The objective of training the <span id="S4.SS4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">HRCL</span> framework is to optimize the parameters of deep neural networks representing agents’ policies so they can reliably achieve high rewards across multiple episodes. Each episode reflects a complete cycle of plan formulation and decision-making over a temporal horizon. Once the training process is complete, the learned policies are deployed as the execution mechanism for <span id="S4.SS4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">HRCL</span>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">As illustrated in Fig. <a href="#S3.F1" title="Fig. 1 ‣ III-B Problem Formulation ‣ III System Model ‣ Strategic Coordination for Evolving Multi-agent Systems:A Hierarchical Reinforcement and Collective Learning Approach" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, <span id="S4.SS4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">HRCL</span> adopts a centralized training with decentralized execution paradigm. During training, agents have access to the joint state-action-reward information from all agents, facilitating effective policy updates. However, during execution, each agent operates independently, relying only on its own observations. This design supports real-world deployment by ensuring the system remains decentralized in practice. Training is facilitated through a centralized experience buffer stored in a central server, where each agent contributes its transitions in the form of tuples <math id="S4.SS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(S^{u}_{t},A^{u}_{t},R^{u}_{t},S^{u}_{t+1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(S^{u}_{t},A^{u}_{t},R^{u}_{t},S^{u}_{t+1})</annotation></semantics></math>. At regular intervals, i.e., every <math id="S4.SS4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> episodes, a subset of these transitions <math id="S4.SS4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(S^{u}_{h},A^{u}_{h},R^{u}_{h},S^{u}_{h+1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>h</mi><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>h</mi><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>h</mi><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(S^{u}_{h},A^{u}_{h},R^{u}_{h},S^{u}_{h+1})</annotation></semantics></math> is randomly sampled to train the deep neutral networks via mini-batch learning.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">To enhance learning performance, <span id="S4.SS4.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">HRCL</span> utilizes an actor-critic architecture that combines the strengths of policy-based and value-based methods <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib33" title="" class="ltx_ref">33</a>]</cite>. Each agent is equipped with two deep neural networks: (1) A centralized critic <math id="S4.SS4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> at central server, which assesses the quality of selected actions; (2) An actor <math id="S4.SS4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> at each agent, which defines the agent’s policy and determines its next action. This setup allows the actor to learn directly from gradient feedback while the critic provides stabilizing value estimates. To further reinforce stability and prevent overly aggressive policy updates, <span id="S4.SS4.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">HRCL</span> incorporates Proximal Policy Optimization (PPO) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib34" title="" class="ltx_ref">34</a>]</cite>, a widely used method for regularizing policy changes.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS4.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS4.p4.1" class="ltx_p">During critic updates, the system calculates the advantage of an action using the Bellman-based temporal difference:</p>
<table id="S4.E9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{A}^{u}_{h}=R^{u}_{h}+\gamma\cdot Q(S^{u}_{h+1},A^{u}_{h+1})-Q(S^{u}_{h},A^{u}_{h})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>h</mi><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>h</mi><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>h</mi><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{A}^{u}_{h}=R^{u}_{h}+\gamma\cdot Q(S^{u}_{h+1},A^{u}_{h+1})-Q(S^{u}_{h},A^{u}_{h}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS4.p4.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S4.SS4.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> is a discount factor to balance long-term and immediate rewards, which is empirically determined by the system; <math id="S4.SS4.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S^{u}_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>h</mi><mi>u</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S^{u}_{h}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS4.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{u}_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>h</mi><mi>u</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{u}_{h}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the state and the action of agent <math id="S4.SS4.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> in the sampled experience batch. This advantage value <math id="S4.SS4.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{A}^{u}_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi><mi>u</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{A}^{u}_{h}</annotation></semantics></math> is then passed to the actor network to encourage beneficial actions (high reward) and discourage less effective ones (low reward). Actions are generated by the policy as <math id="S4.SS4.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{u}_{t}=\pi(S^{u}_{t}|\theta^{\pi})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mi>π</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{u}_{t}=\pi(S^{u}_{t}|\theta^{\pi})</annotation></semantics></math> and updated using the clipped objective of PPO, which stabilizes learning by constraining the policy update ratio:</p>
<table id="S4.E10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{prob}(\theta^{\pi},u)=\frac{\pi_{\theta^{\pi}}(A^{u}_{h}|S^{u}_{h})}{\pi_{old}(A^{u}_{h}|S^{u}_{h})}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>prob</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mi>π</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mi>π</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>h</mi><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>h</mi><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>h</mi><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>h</mi><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{prob}(\theta^{\pi},u)=\frac{\pi_{\theta^{\pi}}(A^{u}_{h}|S^{u}_{h})}{\pi_{old}(A^{u}_{h}|S^{u}_{h})},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS4.p4.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S4.SS4.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{old}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{old}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the policy of actor network from the previous iteration. This ratio is used in surrogate loss function:</p>
<table id="S4.E11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{C}^{u}_{h}=\min[\text{prob}(\theta^{\pi},u)\cdot\hat{A}^{u}_{h},\;\text{clip}(\text{prob}(\theta^{\pi},u),1-\epsilon,1+\epsilon)\cdot\hat{A}^{u}_{h}]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>prob</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mi>π</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi><mi>u</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>clip</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext>prob</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mi>π</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi><mi>u</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{C}^{u}_{h}=\min[\text{prob}(\theta^{\pi},u)\cdot\hat{A}^{u}_{h},\;\text{clip}(\text{prob}(\theta^{\pi},u),1-\epsilon,1+\epsilon)\cdot\hat{A}^{u}_{h}],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS4.p4.4" class="ltx_p">with the hyperparameter <math id="S4.SS4.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> and the clipping method <math id="S4.SS4.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{clip}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>clip</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{clip}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> serving as a clipping threshold to limit how far the policy is allowed to change, ensuring conservative updates. Finally, the actor and critic parameters, <math id="S4.SS4.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta^{\pi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>θ</mi><mi>π</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta^{\pi}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS4.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta^{Q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>θ</mi><mi>Q</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta^{Q}</annotation></semantics></math>, are optimized by minimizing their respective loss functions:</p>
<table id="S4.E12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{\text{actor}}(\theta^{\pi})=\frac{1}{U\cdot H}\sum_{u=1}^{U}\sum_{h=1}^{H}\hat{C}^{u}_{h}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mtext>actor</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mi>π</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>U</mi></munderover><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>H</mi></munderover><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi><mi>u</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{\text{actor}}(\theta^{\pi})=\frac{1}{U\cdot H}\sum_{u=1}^{U}\sum_{h=1}^{H}\hat{C}^{u}_{h},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="S4.E13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{\text{critic}}(\theta^{Q})=\frac{1}{U\cdot H}\sum^{U}_{u=1}\sum^{H}_{h=1}(\hat{A}^{u}_{h})^{2}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mtext>critic</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mi>Q</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>U</mi></munderover><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>H</mi></munderover><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{\text{critic}}(\theta^{Q})=\frac{1}{U\cdot H}\sum^{U}_{u=1}\sum^{H}_{h=1}(\hat{A}^{u}_{h})^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS4.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS4.p5.1" class="ltx_p">In summary, the training process primarily involves the following steps (see Algorithm <a href="#alg1" title="In IV-C Low-level Plan Selection ‣ IV Proposed Method ‣ Strategic Coordination for Evolving Multi-agent Systems:A Hierarchical Reinforcement and Collective Learning Approach" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>): It firstly performs the network initialization to set parameters in actor and critic networks within <math id="S4.SS4.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[-0.1,0.1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>0.1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>0.1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[-0.1,0.1]</annotation></semantics></math> (Line 1). Next, in the exploration part (Lines 3-17) in each episode, each agent takes actions to choose a constraint of plans and a range of behavior. After coordination in low-level plan generation and plan selection, agents calculate their immediate rewards and transition to a new state. The buffer, a data storage structure used for experience replay, stores all the transitions of each agent (Line 14). For every <math id="S4.SS4.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> episodes, which equals to the batch size, <math id="S4.SS4.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> groups of transitions are randomly sampled from the buffer (Line 15). Finally, the algorithm updates the parameters in critic network <math id="S4.SS4.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta^{Q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>θ</mi><mi>Q</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta^{Q}</annotation></semantics></math> and actor network <math id="S4.SS4.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta^{\pi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>θ</mi><mi>π</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta^{\pi}</annotation></semantics></math> (Lines 18-21).</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS4.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS4.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Moreover, the decentralized execution process is illustrated in Algorithm <a href="#alg2" title="In IV-C Low-level Plan Selection ‣ IV Proposed Method ‣ Strategic Coordination for Evolving Multi-agent Systems:A Hierarchical Reinforcement and Collective Learning Approach" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>. With the input of initial target <math id="S4.SS4.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, policy function <math id="S4.SS4.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> and high-level strategy, each agent runs the algorithm and outputs <math id="S4.SS4.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{u}_{st}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>u</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{u}_{st}</annotation></semantics></math> at each time period. Finally, each agent obtains its plans for all periods and execute them.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S5" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">V </span><span id="S5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Experimental Methodology</span></h2>

<div id="S5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This section defines the hyperparameters of the proposed approach. The metrics and baselines used for the performance evaluation are introduced. The computation and communication complexity of all methods are also compared.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S5.F3" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.18088v1/Targets.svg" id="S5.F3.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/175;" width="476" height="175"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Fig. 3: </span>Synthetic target tasks for all agents of cosine waveforms by increasing the frequency multipliers <math id="S5.F3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ω</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega</annotation></semantics></math>.</figcaption>
</figure>
<section id="S5.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S5.SS1.4" class="ltx_text">V-A</span> </span><span id="S5.SS1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Scenario Settings</span></h3>

<div id="S5.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The synthetic scenario is built by extracting data from the synthetic dataset <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib35" title="" class="ltx_ref">35</a>]</cite>. It contains <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1,000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1,000</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1,000</annotation></semantics></math> agents, each with <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="16" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>16</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">16</annotation></semantics></math> possible plans (i.e., vectors) that consists of a sequence of <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="100" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>100</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">100</annotation></semantics></math> values sampled from a Normal distribution centered at a mean of 0 with a variance of 1. The discomfort costs of plans for each agent are increasing linearly within the range <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>. The plans are grouped using the quantile-based discretization function based on their discomfort cost.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The goal of the optimization is to bring the global plan close to a target signal (a cosine waveform) over <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="16" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>16</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">16</annotation></semantics></math> time periods, while minimizing the discomfort cost of all agents. At each time period <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, the update of the target can be formulated as: <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{t+1}=\tau_{t}-g_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{t+1}=\tau_{t}-g_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> represents the target signal of the cosine waveform. Note that agents predict the future shape of waveform they construct (i.e., the global plan), which gradually approaches <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, updates the target, and thus the environment “seen” by each agent is evolving. Moreover, to increase the complexity of targets, the frequency multiplier of the cosine waveforms increases, as shown in Fig. <a href="#S5.F3" title="Fig. 3 ‣ V Experimental Methodology ‣ Strategic Coordination for Evolving Multi-agent Systems:A Hierarchical Reinforcement and Collective Learning Approach" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>. The cross-validation is applied: <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="80\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>80</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">80\%</annotation></semantics></math> plans of the datasets for training and <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="20\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>20</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">20\%</annotation></semantics></math> for testing. This makes the global plan differentiated in each test and the task environment dynamically changing.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">There are two types of scenarios: (1) <em id="S5.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Basic synthetic scenario.</em> It is a benchmark with <math id="S5.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="40" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>40</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">40</annotation></semantics></math> agents, <math id="S5.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="16" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>16</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">16</annotation></semantics></math> time periods, <math id="S5.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="16" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>16</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">16</annotation></semantics></math> plans per agent and the target signal of <math id="S5.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega=\pi/24" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>24</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega=\pi/24</annotation></semantics></math>, aiming to compare the performance of different approaches. (2) <em id="S5.SS1.p3.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Complex synthetic scenarios.</em> They are studied by varying the parameters to validate the scalability of the proposed solution. There are three dimensions: (1) number of agents, (2) number of plans (i.e., the plan volume owned by each agent), and (3) complexity of target tasks (i.e., different frequency multipliers of cosine waveforms).</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Apart from synthetic scenarios, this paper studies two smart city application scenarios: energy self-management (Section <a href="#S6.SS2" title="VI-B Evaluation on energy self-management ‣ VI Performance Evaluation ‣ Strategic Coordination for Evolving Multi-agent Systems:A Hierarchical Reinforcement and Collective Learning Approach" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">VI-B</span></a>) and drone swarm sensing (Section <a href="#S6.SS3" title="VI-C Evaluation on drone swarm sensing ‣ VI Performance Evaluation ‣ Strategic Coordination for Evolving Multi-agent Systems:A Hierarchical Reinforcement and Collective Learning Approach" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">VI-C</span></a>). Table <a href="#S5.T3" title="TABLE III ‣ V-A Scenario Settings ‣ V Experimental Methodology ‣ Strategic Coordination for Evolving Multi-agent Systems:A Hierarchical Reinforcement and Collective Learning Approach" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">III</span></a> shows the comparison of parameter settings among different scenarios.</p>
</div>
