<section id="S5.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S5.SS2.4" class="ltx_text">V-B</span> </span><span id="S5.SS2.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Metrics and Baselines</span></h3>

<div id="S5.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To evaluate the performance of <em id="S5.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">HRCL</em>, we introduce two metrics: (1) Mean discomfort cost, which denotes the average of discomfort cost of all agents, defined in Eq.(<a href="#S3.E3" title="In III-B Problem Formulation ‣ III System Model ‣ Strategic Coordination for Evolving Multi-agent Systems:A Hierarchical Reinforcement and Collective Learning Approach" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>); (2) Inefficiency cost, which calculates the root mean square error (RMSE) between the target and global plan, defined in Eq.(<a href="#S3.E4" title="In III-B Problem Formulation ‣ III System Model ‣ Strategic Coordination for Evolving Multi-agent Systems:A Hierarchical Reinforcement and Collective Learning Approach" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>); and (3) Combined cost, which measures the sum of the normalized mean discomfort cost and inefficiency cost. In simple words, the mean discomfort cost measures the cost of agents who execute the system tasks, while the inefficiency cost measures the overall quality of the executed system tasks. Combined cost provides a comprehensive assessment of the performance of <em id="S5.SS2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">HRCL</em>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">A fair comparison of the proposed methods with related work is not straightforward as there is a very limited number of relevant decentralized algorithms <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">14</a>, <a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">15</a>, <a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">17</a>]</cite>. Similar algorithms, such as particle swarm optimization, cannot be directly applicable to the optimization problem defined in Section <a href="#S3" title="III System Model ‣ Strategic Coordination for Evolving Multi-agent Systems:A Hierarchical Reinforcement and Collective Learning Approach" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">III</span></a>. Those relevant algorithms (e.g., COHDA, CBBA) have higher computational and communication overhead than the collective learning used in <em id="S5.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">HRCL</em> (see Section <a href="#S6.SS1" title="VI-A Evaluation on synthetic scenario ‣ VI Performance Evaluation ‣ Strategic Coordination for Evolving Multi-agent Systems:A Hierarchical Reinforcement and Collective Learning Approach" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">VI-A</span></a>). For this reason, this chapter focuses on ablation studies by testing standalone reinforcement learning, collective learning and exact algorithms. The baseline methods are introduced as:</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">(1) <em id="S5.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">EPOS</em>: The name is Economic Planning and Optimized Selections <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">2</a>]</cite>, a decentralized collective learning designed to coordinate agents to select a plan from the set <math id="S5.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}^{u}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>u</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}^{u}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> via Eq.(<a href="#S3.E5" title="In III-B Problem Formulation ‣ III System Model ‣ Strategic Coordination for Evolving Multi-agent Systems:A Hierarchical Reinforcement and Collective Learning Approach" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>). It incorporates the plan generation and the target update, but does not support any long-term strategic decision on task planning via learning methods. Moreover, the agents’ behaviors <math id="S5.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta^{u}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>u</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta^{u}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> in the algorithm are assumed to be the same.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">(2) <em id="S5.SS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">MAPPO</em>: The name is Multi-Agent Proximal Policy Optimization, a state-of-the-art MARL technique <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib34" title="" class="ltx_ref">34</a>]</cite>. It is adapted based on the designed model that each agent takes an action to choose one plan from the set <math id="S5.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P^{u}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>u</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P^{u}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, its action space equals to the total number of plans generated by each agent <math id="S5.SS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum^{I}_{i=1}G_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>I</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum^{I}_{i=1}G_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. It employs the reward function of Eq.(<a href="#S4.E6" title="In IV-A MARL modeling ‣ IV Proposed Method ‣ Strategic Coordination for Evolving Multi-agent Systems:A Hierarchical Reinforcement and Collective Learning Approach" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>), the actor-critic networks and proximal policy optimization. There is no high-level strategies for group choices but only address low-level plan selection.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">(3) <em id="S5.SS2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">HRL: It is adapted based on the Hierarchical Reinforcement Learning</em> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">17</a>]</cite> and designed model that each agent takes an action for high-level choices of plan constraints and then takes a second action to select a plan under the chosen constraint (i.e., low-level plan selection ). The policy networks of both types of actions are trained independently by using two different actor networks.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Furthermore, two variants of the proposed <em id="S5.SS2.p6.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">HRCL</em> are considered: (1) <em id="S5.SS2.p6.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">HRCL-P</em>, which uses the strategy for <em id="S5.SS2.p6.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">grouping plan constraints</em> only and sets the agents’ behaviors the same, and (2) <em id="S5.SS2.p6.1.4" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">HRCL-B</em>, which uses the strategy for <em id="S5.SS2.p6.1.5" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">grouping behavior ranges</em> only where agents select plans from the whole set <math id="S5.SS2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}^{u}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>u</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}^{u}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>. As a comparison, <em id="S5.SS2.p6.1.6" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">HRCL</em> takes both strategies together.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S5.SS3.4" class="ltx_text">V-C</span> </span><span id="S5.SS3.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Algorithm Settings</span></h3>

<div id="S5.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The setting of the proposed approach contains both DCL and MARL parts:</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">During the coordinated plan selection via <em id="S5.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">EPOS</em><span id="footnote2" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">2</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">2</sup>
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">2</span>
              
              
            Available at: https://github.com/epournaras/EPOS.</span></span></span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">2</a>, <a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">3</a>]</cite>, the communication structure among agents is set as a balanced binary tree <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib31" title="" class="ltx_ref">31</a>]</cite>. In the one execution of <em id="S5.SS3.p2.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">EPOS</em>, the agents perform <math id="S5.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="20" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>20</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">20</annotation></semantics></math> bottom-up and top-down learning iterations. In addition, several variants of <em id="S5.SS3.p2.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">EPOS</em> are also defined: (1) <em id="S5.SS3.p2.1.4" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">EPOS-altruistic</em> that agents behave altruistically (<math id="S5.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta^{u}_{t}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta^{u}_{t}=0</annotation></semantics></math>), (2) <em id="S5.SS3.p2.1.5" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">EPOS-selfish</em> that agents behave selfishly (<math id="S5.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta^{u}_{t}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta^{u}_{t}=1</annotation></semantics></math>), and 3) <em id="S5.SS3.p2.1.6" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">EPOS-P</em> that agents choose the Pareto optimal point of behavior value.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">For the reinforcement learning in <em id="S5.SS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">HRCL</em>, a total of <math id="S5.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H=64" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>64</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H=64</annotation></semantics></math> transitions are sampled as a batch in a replay buffer with a discount factor of <math id="S5.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma=0.95" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.95</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma=0.95</annotation></semantics></math> and a clip interval hyperparameter of <math id="S5.SS3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.2</annotation></semantics></math> for policy updating. We use the recurrent neural network (RNN), and use <math id="S5.SS3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W=64" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>64</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W=64</annotation></semantics></math> neurons in the two hidden layers of the RNN in both critic and actor networks. The activation function used for the networks is tanh. The models are trained over <math id="S5.SS3.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}=2000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2000</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}=2000</annotation></semantics></math> episodes, each consisting of multiple time periods. Furthermore, our approach employs Proximal Policy Optimization to prevent detrimental updates and improving the stability of the learning process <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib34" title="" class="ltx_ref">34</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Furthermore, several parameters in the proposed methods are empirically selected due to the optimal performance: <em id="S5.SS3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">HRCL-P</em> divides plans into <math id="S5.SS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4</annotation></semantics></math> groups, each containing <math id="S5.SS3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4</annotation></semantics></math> plans; <em id="S5.SS3.p4.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">HRCL-B</em> divides the behavior range into <math id="S5.SS3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4</annotation></semantics></math> ranges; and <em id="S5.SS3.p4.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">HRCL</em> groups both <math id="S5.SS3.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4</annotation></semantics></math> plans and <math id="S5.SS3.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4</annotation></semantics></math> behavior ranges. The agent behavior is set as <math id="S5.SS3.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta^{u}_{t}=0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta^{u}_{t}=0.5</annotation></semantics></math> in both <em id="S5.SS3.p4.1.4" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">EPOS</em> and <em id="S5.SS3.p4.1.5" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">HRCL</em>. The <math id="S5.SS3.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS3.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> in Eq.(<a href="#S4.E6" title="In IV-A MARL modeling ‣ IV Proposed Method ‣ Strategic Coordination for Evolving Multi-agent Systems:A Hierarchical Reinforcement and Collective Learning Approach" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>) are set as <math id="S5.SS3.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.5</annotation></semantics></math> such that the reward is equivalent to the metric of combined cost defined in Section <a href="#S5.SS2" title="V-B Metrics and Baselines ‣ V Experimental Methodology ‣ Strategic Coordination for Evolving Multi-agent Systems:A Hierarchical Reinforcement and Collective Learning Approach" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">V-B</span></a>. The effect of different parameters are illustrated in Fig. <a href="#S6.F5.sf4" title="In Fig. 5 ‣ VI Performance Evaluation ‣ Strategic Coordination for Evolving Multi-agent Systems:A Hierarchical Reinforcement and Collective Learning Approach" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5(d)</span></a>, <a href="#S6.F5.sf5" title="In Fig. 5 ‣ VI Performance Evaluation ‣ Strategic Coordination for Evolving Multi-agent Systems:A Hierarchical Reinforcement and Collective Learning Approach" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5(e)</span></a> and <a href="#S6.F5.sf6" title="In Fig. 5 ‣ VI Performance Evaluation ‣ Strategic Coordination for Evolving Multi-agent Systems:A Hierarchical Reinforcement and Collective Learning Approach" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5(f)</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S6" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">VI </span><span id="S6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Performance Evaluation</span></h2>

<div id="S6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, the synthetic scenario is used to validate the superior performance of the proposed <em id="S6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">HRCL</em>. Additionally, this section shows the broad and significant impact of the proposed generic algorithm on two very different scenarios in the context of smart grids and smart cities: (1) Energy self-management and (2) drone swarm sensing.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S6.F4" class="ltx_figure ltx_align_center">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Fig. 4: </span>Cost comparison of all methods in the basic synthetic scenario (<math id="S6.F4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="40" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>40</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">40</annotation></semantics></math> agents, <math id="S6.F4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="16" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>16</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">16</annotation></semantics></math> plans per agent and the target signal with <math id="S6.F4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega=\pi/24" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>24</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega=\pi/24</annotation></semantics></math>). The vertical lines denote the error.</figcaption><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.18088v1/Basic.svg" id="S6.F4.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/172;" width="476" height="172"></object>
</figure>
<figure id="S6.T4" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering" style="font-size:80%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">TABLE IV: </span>Comparison of computational and communication costs.</figcaption>
<div id="S6.T4.3" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:345.0pt;height:70.1pt;vertical-align:-33.4pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-37.4pt,7.6pt) scale(0.82197239973419,0.82197239973419) ;">
<table id="S6.T4.3.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="S6.T4.3.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S6.T4.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_th_row ltx_border_tt"><span id="S6.T4.3.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">Approaches:</span></th>
<th id="S6.T4.3.1.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="S6.T4.3.1.1.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">Computational Cost</span></th>
<th id="S6.T4.3.1.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="S6.T4.3.1.1.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">Communication Cost</span></th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="S6.T4.3.1.2" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S6.T4.3.1.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_t"><em id="S6.T4.3.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:80%;">MAPPO</em><span id="S6.T4.3.1.2.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;"> </span><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><span id="S6.T4.3.1.2.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">[</span><a href="#bib.bib34" title="" class="ltx_ref">34</a><span id="S6.T4.3.1.2.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">]</span></cite></th>
<td id="S6.T4.3.1.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><math id="S6.T4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\mathcal{E}\cdot T\cdot U\cdot C_{\text{dnn}}(K))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.800em">ℰ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">T</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">U</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.800em">C</mi><mtext mathsize="0.800em">dnn</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">K</mi><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\mathcal{E}\cdot T\cdot U\cdot C_{\text{dnn}}(K))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S6.T4.3.1.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><math id="S6.T4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\mathcal{E}\cdot T\cdot U^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.800em">ℰ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">T</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.800em">U</mi><mn mathsize="0.800em">2</mn></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\mathcal{E}\cdot T\cdot U^{2})</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="S6.T4.3.1.3" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S6.T4.3.1.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row"><em id="S6.T4.3.1.3.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:80%;">HRL</em><span id="S6.T4.3.1.3.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;"> </span><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><span id="S6.T4.3.1.3.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">[</span><a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">17</a><span id="S6.T4.3.1.3.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">]</span></cite></th>
<td id="S6.T4.3.1.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.T4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\mathcal{E}\cdot T\cdot U\cdot C_{\text{dnn}}(I+\frac{K}{I}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.800em">ℰ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">T</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">U</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.800em">C</mi><mtext mathsize="0.800em">dnn</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">(</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">I</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">+</mo><mfrac><mi mathsize="0.800em">K</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">I</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\mathcal{E}\cdot T\cdot U\cdot C_{\text{dnn}}(I+\frac{K}{I}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S6.T4.3.1.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.T4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\mathcal{E}\cdot T\cdot U^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.800em">ℰ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">T</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.800em">U</mi><mn mathsize="0.800em">2</mn></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\mathcal{E}\cdot T\cdot U^{2})</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="S6.T4.3.1.4" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S6.T4.3.1.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row"><em id="S6.T4.3.1.4.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:80%;">EPOS <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">2</a>]</cite></em></th>
<td id="S6.T4.3.1.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.T4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(T\cdot K\cdot L\log U)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">(</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">T</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">K</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">L</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">U</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(T\cdot K\cdot L\log U)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S6.T4.3.1.4.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.T4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(T\cdot L\cdot\log U)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">(</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">T</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">L</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">U</mi></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(T\cdot L\cdot\log U)</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="S6.T4.3.1.5" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S6.T4.3.1.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row"><em id="S6.T4.3.1.5.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:80%;">HRCL-P</em></th>
<td id="S6.T4.3.1.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.T4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\mathcal{E}\cdot T\cdot(U\cdot C_{\text{dnn}}(I)+\frac{K}{I}\cdot L\cdot\log U))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.800em">ℰ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">T</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">U</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.800em">C</mi><mtext mathsize="0.800em">dnn</mtext></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">I</mi><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.800em">+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi mathsize="0.800em">K</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">I</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">L</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">U</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\mathcal{E}\cdot T\cdot(U\cdot C_{\text{dnn}}(I)+\frac{K}{I}\cdot L\cdot\log U))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S6.T4.3.1.5.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.T4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\mathcal{E}\cdot T\cdot L\cdot\log U)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.800em">ℰ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">T</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">L</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">U</mi></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\mathcal{E}\cdot T\cdot L\cdot\log U)</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="S6.T4.3.1.6" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S6.T4.3.1.6.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row"><em id="S6.T4.3.1.6.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:80%;">HRCL-B</em></th>
<td id="S6.T4.3.1.6.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.T4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\mathcal{E}\cdot T\cdot(U\cdot C_{\text{dnn}}(M)+K\cdot L\cdot\log U))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.800em">ℰ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">T</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">U</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.800em">C</mi><mtext mathsize="0.800em">dnn</mtext></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">M</mi><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.800em">+</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">K</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">L</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">U</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\mathcal{E}\cdot T\cdot(U\cdot C_{\text{dnn}}(M)+K\cdot L\cdot\log U))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S6.T4.3.1.6.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.T4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\mathcal{E}\cdot T\cdot L\cdot\log U)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.800em">ℰ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">T</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">L</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">U</mi></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\mathcal{E}\cdot T\cdot L\cdot\log U)</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="S6.T4.3.1.7" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S6.T4.3.1.7.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_bb"><em id="S6.T4.3.1.7.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:80%;">HRCL</em></th>
<td id="S6.T4.3.1.7.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb"><math id="S6.T4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\mathcal{E}\cdot T\cdot(U\cdot C_{\text{dnn}}(I\cdot M)+\frac{K}{I}\cdot L\cdot\log U))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.800em">ℰ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">T</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">U</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.800em">C</mi><mtext mathsize="0.800em">dnn</mtext></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">(</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">I</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">M</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.800em">+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi mathsize="0.800em">K</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">I</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">L</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">U</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\mathcal{E}\cdot T\cdot(U\cdot C_{\text{dnn}}(I\cdot M)+\frac{K}{I}\cdot L\cdot\log U))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S6.T4.3.1.7.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb"><math id="S6.T4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\mathcal{E}\cdot T\cdot L\cdot\log U)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.800em">ℰ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">T</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">L</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">U</mi></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\mathcal{E}\cdot T\cdot L\cdot\log U)</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</span></div>
</figure>
